  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 127 AM CDT Mon Aug 17 2026\n\nWednesday morning, we may continue to see residual showers/storms as \nthe cold front fully exits the area. At this point, the severe \nthreat will be quite limited. Thus, we are not expecting many \nimpacts at that point. Post-frontal airmass will kick in Wednesday, \nwith light northeasterly winds and decreasing cloud cover. The \nremainder of the work week seems to be quiet, with a slightly cooler \nairmass in place and much lower humidity. We will remain under weak \nnorthwesterly flow aloft, with a few weak impulses in the flow.\nAlthough, with low moisture and lacking return flow, we are not\nexpecting much rain for the rest of the week. As was mentioned \nin the previous discussion, any precipitation will largely be \nin the form of isolated instability showers. A few global models\nindicate chances late Friday into Saturday morning, but \nconfidence is low on this. Will stick with what the NBM\ninitialized, introducing 15-30% PoPs Friday evening/night. \nOtherwise, a much needed stretch of mostly-dry weather will be \nseen, with comfortable humidity and temperatures largely in the \nupper 70s.",
